          %h2#in_quantum_mechanics In quantum mechanics
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            what is called the
            %em Dyson formula
            is what in
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            is called the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+integral"}> iterated integral
                \-expression for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi t
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi i
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{d}{d t} \psi(t)
                  \\;=\;
                  i H(t)
                  \\psi(t)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \mapsto \psi(t) \in \mathcal{H}
            is a one-parameter family of elements of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \mapsto H(t)
            is a one-parameter family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operators"} linear operators
            on this Hilbert space.
          %p
            This appears prominently in the expression of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} Schrödinger equation
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction+picture"} interaction picture
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(t)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+picture"} Heisenberg picture
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            theory. In this case the Dyson series gives the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+picture"} Schrödinger picture
          %p
            The idea is to think of the solution as given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi id
                          %mo +
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mi N
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi id
                          %mo +
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mi N
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi N
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi id
                          %mo +
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mi N
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext factors
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi(t)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\underset{N \to \infty}{\lim}
                  \\underset{N \, \text{factors}}{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\left(
                  id + \tfrac{i}{N}H(t)
                  \\right)
                  \\left(
                  id + \tfrac{i}{N}H(t(N-1)/N)
                  \\right)
                  \\cdots
                  \\left(
                  id + \tfrac{i}{N}H(t/N)
                  \\right)
                  }
                  }
                  \\psi(0)
          %p
            and to think of this as the result of forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential"} exponential
            expression
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\int_{[0,t] } H(t)\,d t)
            and then re-ordering in the resulting sum of products all the factors of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(t)
            such that they are
            %em time ordered
            with larger values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            ordered to the left of smaller values.
          %p Accordingly, in the physics literature solutions to this equation are written
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi T
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi exp
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi i
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mi t
                      %mo )
                    %mo )
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi(t)
                  \\;=\;
                  T\left(
                  \\exp\left(
                  \\int_{[0,t]} i H(t) \,d t
                  \\right)
                  \\right)
                  \\psi(0)
                  \\,,
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(-)
            the
            %em time ordering operator
            producing
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/series"} series
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+integrals"} iterated integrals
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %munder
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ≤
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi t
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi(t)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\left(
                  \\underoverset{n = 0}{\infty}{\sum}
                  (i)^n
                  \\underset{0 \leq t_1 \leq \cdots \leq t_n \leq t}{\int}
                  H(t_n) H(t_{n-1})\cdots H(t_1)
                  \\right)\psi(0)
          %p
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Dyson series
          %h2#in_quantum_field_theory In quantum field theory
          %p
            The idea generalizes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+field+theory"} relativistic field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            if due care is exercised (including
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adiabatic+switching"} adiabatic switching
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-extension+of+distributions"} point extension
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator-valued+distributions"} operator-valued distributions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+locality"} causal ordering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+algebra"} interacting field algebra
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+product"} time-ordered product
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            for details.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#kontsevich_integral_is_dyson_formula_of_kzconnection Kontsevich integral is Dyson formula of KZ-connection
          %div
            %p
              For the Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection"}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
              we need the following notation:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{\mathrm{f}} \in \mathbb{N}
                  write
                #eq:OrderedConfigurationSpaceofnPointsinC.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi Conf
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi N
                                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo \
                        %mi FatDiagonal
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        (\mathbb{R}^2)^n \backslash FatDiagonal
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+configuration+space+of+n+points"} ordered configuration space of n points
                  in the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                %p
                  Identifying the plane with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℂ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
                #eq:CoordinateFunctionsOnConfC.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi z
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mi Conf
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (z_1, \cdots, z_{N_{\mathrm{f}}})
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,n\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathbb{C}^{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                #eq:HorizontalChordDiagrams.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒜
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi pb
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Span
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi 𝒟
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi pb
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 4
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        Span\big(\mathcal{D}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}\big)/4T
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+vector+space"} quotient vector space
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+span"} linear span
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  strands by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4T+relations"} 4T relations
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+braid+relations"}> infinitesimal braid relations
                  ), regarded as an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                  under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concatenation"} concatenation
                  of strands (
                  %a{:href => "horizontal+chord+diagram#AlgebraOfHorizontalChordDiagrams"}> here
                  ).
            #KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnection.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"}> Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                  )
              %p
                The
                %em
                  universal
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                is the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} algebra valued differential form
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HorizontalChordDiagrams"} (3)
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:OrderedConfigurationSpaceofnPointsinC"} (1)
              #eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pb
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\Omega
                      \\big(
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\,,
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\big)
              %p
                given in the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CoordinateFunctionsOnConfC"} (2)
                by:
              #eq:DefineUniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\underset{ i \lt j \in \{1, \cdots, n\} }{\sum}
                      d_{dR} log\big( z_i - z_j \big)
                      \\otimes t_{i j}
                      \\,,
              %p where
              %center
                %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HorizontalChordGenerator.jpg", :width => "500 /> "}/
              %p
                is the horizontal chord diagram with exactly one chord, which stretches between the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              %p
                Regarded as a connection form for a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+vector+bundle"} connection on a vector bundle
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∇
                          %mi KZ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_{KZ}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant derivative
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KV
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\nabla \phi
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      d \phi + \omega_{KV} \wedge \phi
              %p
                for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pb
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi \;\colon\;
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\longrightarrow
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pb}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}} Mod
              %p
                with values in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over the algebra of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} modulo
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4T+relations"} 4T relations
              %p The condition of covariant constancy
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi KZ
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\nabla_{KZ} \phi \;=\; 0
              %p
                is called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equation
              %p
                Finally, given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %msub
                        %mi Rep
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (
                      V_1,
                      \\cdots,
                      V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      )
                      \\;\in\; (\mathfrak{g} Rep_{/\sim})^{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\,,
              %p
                the corresponding
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi V
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi pf
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi End
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      w_{V}
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\mathcal{A}^{{}^{pf}}_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}
                      \\longrightarrow
                      End_{\mathfrak{g}}\big( V_1 \otimes \cdots V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}}  \big)
              %p
                turns the universal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+form"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov form
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm"} (4)
                into a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+differential+form"} valued differential form
              #eq:LieKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi KZ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %munder
                        %mi Conf
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi N
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} f
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\omega_{KZ}
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\underset{ i \lt j \in \{1, \cdots, n\} }{\sum}
                      d_{dR} log\big( z_i - z_j \big)
                      \\otimes w_V(t_{i j})
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\Omega
                      \\big(
                      \\underset{{}^{\{1,\cdots,N_{\mathrm{f}}\}}}{Conf}(\mathbb{C})
                      \\,,
                      End\big(V_1 \otimes \cdot V_{N_{\mathrm{f}}} \big)
                      \\big)
                      
                      \\,.
            %p
              The universal formulation
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalKnizhnikZamolodchikovForm"} (4)
              is highlighted for instance in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Vassiliev+invariant#BarNatan95"} Bat-Natan 95, Section 4.2
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Kontsevich+integral#Lescop00"} Lescop 00, p. 7
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Kontsevich+integral#Kohno14"} Kohno 14, Section 5
            #KnizhnikZamolodchikovConnectionIsFlat.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
                  is
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat
              %p
